Subject: [PATCH 2/2] autotests: A window that declares stereo content is told
 its depth limits

testStereoDepthLimits: the property holds the limits of the output as the
Wayland event's fixed point values, follows a change of the settings, is absent
on a window that declares nothing, goes when the declaration is withdrawn and
comes back when it is made again. The announced support is 10.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
